IMPORT prelude

-- A New Tax System (Family Assistance) Act 1999 (Cth) -- what family payments and child care subsidy a parent can get for
-- a child: the immunisation requirements and what failing them does (ss 6, 61B; Sch 1 cll 7(2), 26(3)); who is an FTB child
-- and who is eligible for Family Tax Benefit (ss 21, 22, 26); the FTB Part A rate by Method 1 and Method 2 (Sch 1 cll 1-4,
-- 7, 25, 25D, 26, 28, 38A, 38L-38N); the FTB Part B rate (Sch 1 cll 28B-29, 30, 31A, 32, 33; Sch 3 cl 3); the newborn
-- supplement (Sch 1 cl 35A, parent route) and the newborn upfront payment (s 58AA); and the Child Care Subsidy: eligibility
-- for a session (s 85BA), the applicable percentage (Sch 2 cll 3, 3A, 3B), the hourly rate (cl 2), subsidised hours (the
-- activity test, cll 11, 12) and the subsidy for a fortnight (cll 1, 4, simplified).
--
-- SEAT: the parent (the claimant) -- "What family payments and child care subsidy can I get for my child?". Every decision
-- is phrased as the parent asks it: "Does my child meet the immunisation requirements?", "Am I eligible for family tax
-- benefit?", "How much FTB Part A do I get a year?", "Do I get the newborn upfront payment?", "What percentage of my child
-- care fees is subsidised?". Where the Act hands a judgment to the Secretary (s 6(6), s 26(2), s 61B(3)), it is asked as a
-- fact the parent can state (a determination has been made; a notice has been given on a date).
--
-- Provisions covered: s 3 (by reference), s 6(2)-(6), s 21(1), s 22(2)-(5), s 26(1), s 58AA(1), (1A), (2), (4), s 61B(1),
-- (2), (4), s 85BA(1); Sch 1 cll 1(1), (2), 2, 3, 4, 7(1), (2), 25, 25D, 26(2), (3), 28, 28B, 28C, 28D(1), (2), 29(1), (2),
-- 30, 31A(1)(a), (2), 32, 33, 35A(2), (8)-(10), 38A(1A)-(3), 38L, 38M, 38N; Sch 2 cll 1, 2(1), (3), 3(1), (4), 3A(1)-(3),
-- (6), 3B(1)-(2) (as two facts), 4(1)(a), (2) (one service, no other CCS hours), 11(1), (1A), 12(1), (1A); Sch 3 cl 3(1),
-- (2).
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 124, compilation date 1 July 2026 (includes amendments up to Act No. 73, 2025), register id
-- C2026C00331, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A00490.txt. No regulation or instrument is deposited:
-- the Child Care Subsidy Minister's Rules 2017 and the immunisation schedules determined under s 4 are not in the deposit,
-- so what they decide (recognised activity hours, the vaccination schedule) is asked as a fact.
--
-- RATES ARE INPUTS. Schedule 4 cl 2 lists as indexed every dollar amount used here except two (the $80,000 FTB Part A
-- supplement limit in Sch 1 cl 38A(1A) and the $450,000 band in Sch 2 cl 3(4)). The figures printed in the compilation are
-- therefore not the figures paid in any given year, and Sch 2 cl 2(3) says its printed caps "reflect the indexation applied
-- on 1 July 2019". Every rate question takes a `Rates` record; `the rates as printed in Compilation No. 124` holds the
-- printed figures, for use as labelled examples. The newborn supplement amounts (Sch 1 cl 35B) and the CCS taper
-- percentages (Sch 2 cll 3(2), 3A(4), (5)) are formulas that did not survive into the deposit ("using the following
-- formula:" and nothing after), so they are inputs too.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the maintenance income test (Sch 1 Div 5); rent assistance; energy supplements (Part A and Part B, closed to
-- new claimants after 19 September 2016 by cll 6A, 25C, 29AA); FTB advances; the multiple birth allowance; the Part B method
-- for a secondary earner returning to work (cll 29A-29D); the cl 29(3) rule disregarding a 16-19 year old FTB child who is
-- not at senior secondary school (the youngest child's age here is that of a child who counts); shared care, percentage of
-- care and blended families (ss 22(7), 22A, 25, 27-29, 35A-35T; cll 11, 27, 31, 31A(1)(b), (c)); the entrustment and
-- adoption routes to the newborn supplement (cl 35A(5)-(7)) and the instrument under cl 35A(12); the stillborn baby payment;
-- the health check reduction (s 61A); the past-period reduction (cll 7(3), 26(4)); s 61D (death of a child); ACCS and Sch 2
-- Part 2; the hourly-session-fee adjustments in cl 2(2) and the adjusted subsidy amount (cl 4A); rounding to the cent (s
-- 58(3), Sch 2 cl 2(1)) -- the cases use figures that need none; Schedule 3 beyond cl 3; Schedule 4 beyond the fact of
-- indexation; the Administration Act (claims, reconciliation, debts). The 1996, 2003 and 2006 events of the lives are
-- answered under this 2026 compilation or not at all: see NOTES.md.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the
-- individual to whom the law is applied, with the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `A New Tax System (Family Assistance) Act 1999`

GIVEN `x` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the positive part of` MEANS
    IF `x` GREATER THAN 0 THEN `x` ELSE 0

GIVEN `percent` IS A NUMBER
      `amount`  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`percent of` MEANS `percent` TIMES `amount` DIVIDED BY 100

-- s 2 / the Act's title: "Act No. 80, 1999". An Act of 1999 cannot answer for a day before 1999; whether it was in force on a
-- later day turns on s 2 (the GST Act commencements), which the deposit does not date.
`the year the Act was made` MEANS 1999

@export Could this Act apply to something that happened in this year?
GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year of the event
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Could this Act apply to my event in that year` IF
    `the year` AT LEAST `the year the Act was made`

§§ `the rates (Schedule 1, Schedule 2, s 58AA; indexed under Schedule 4)`

-- Each field is an amount Schedule 4 cl 2 lists as indexed (its item number in the comment). Gloss: the "FTB child rate" is
-- the yearly amount per child in the standard rate; the "income free area" is the income below which the rate is not
-- reduced; the "CCS hourly rate cap" is the most fee per hour the subsidy is worked on.
DECLARE Rates HAS
    `FTB child rate (A1), child under 13`          IS A NUMBER  -- Sch 1 cl 7(1) item 1; Sch 4 item 1
    `FTB child rate (A1), child 13 or over`        IS A NUMBER  -- Sch 1 cl 7(1) item 2; Sch 4 item 1
    `reduction in FTB child rate`                  IS A NUMBER  -- Sch 1 cll 7(2), 26(3); Sch 4 items 2, 7
    `FTB child rate (A2)`                          IS A NUMBER  -- Sch 1 cl 26(2); Sch 4 item 6
    `FTB gross supplement amount (A)`              IS A NUMBER  -- Sch 1 cl 38A(3); Sch 4 item 8A
    `higher income free area`                      IS A NUMBER  -- Sch 1 cl 2; Sch 4 item 11
    `income free area (A)`                         IS A NUMBER  -- Sch 1 cl 38N; Sch 4 item 13
    `FTB standard rate (B), youngest under 5`      IS A NUMBER  -- Sch 1 cl 30 item 1; Sch 4 item 9
    `FTB standard rate (B), youngest 5 or over`    IS A NUMBER  -- Sch 1 cl 30 item 2; Sch 4 item 9
    `FTB gross supplement amount (B)`              IS A NUMBER  -- Sch 1 cl 31A(2); Sch 4 item 9A
    `income limit (B)`                             IS A NUMBER  -- Sch 1 cl 28B(1); Sch 4 item 17AA
    `income free area (B)`                         IS A NUMBER  -- Sch 1 cl 33; Sch 4 item 14
    `newborn upfront payment`                      IS A NUMBER  -- s 58AA(1); Sch 4 item 7B
    `CCS lower income (base rate) threshold`       IS A NUMBER  -- Sch 2 cl 3(4); Sch 4 item 18
    `CCS lower income (other rate) threshold`      IS A NUMBER  -- Sch 2 cl 3A(6); Sch 4 item 18A
    `CCS hourly rate cap, centre-based day care`   IS A NUMBER  -- Sch 2 cl 2(3) item 1; Sch 4 item 19
    `CCS hourly rate cap, family day care`         IS A NUMBER  -- item 2
    `CCS hourly rate cap, outside school hours care` IS A NUMBER  -- item 3
    `CCS hourly rate cap, in home care`            IS A NUMBER  -- item 4

-- The figures as printed in Compilation No. 124. Not the figures paid in any year (see the header).
`the rates as printed in Compilation No. 124` MEANS Rates WITH
    `FTB child rate (A1), child under 13`          IS 4292.40
    `FTB child rate (A1), child 13 or over`        IS 5580.85
    `reduction in FTB child rate`                  IS 737.30
    `FTB child rate (A2)`                          IS 1416.20
    `FTB gross supplement amount (A)`              IS 600
    `higher income free area`                      IS 98988
    `income free area (A)`                         IS 40000
    `FTB standard rate (B), youngest under 5`      IS 2569.60
    `FTB standard rate (B), youngest 5 or over`    IS 1781.20
    `FTB gross supplement amount (B)`              IS 302.95
    `income limit (B)`                             IS 100000
    `income free area (B)`                         IS 4000
    `newborn upfront payment`                      IS 500
    `CCS lower income (base rate) threshold`       IS 80000
    `CCS lower income (other rate) threshold`      IS 72466
    `CCS hourly rate cap, centre-based day care`   IS 11.98
    `CCS hourly rate cap, family day care`         IS 11.10
    `CCS hourly rate cap, outside school hours care` IS 10.48
    `CCS hourly rate cap, in home care`            IS 32.58

-- Sch 1 cl 38A(1A): the FTB Part A supplement "is nil if the individual's adjusted taxable income is more than $80,000".
-- This $80,000 is NOT in the Schedule 4 cl 2 table (item 18's $80,000 is the CCS threshold in Sch 2 cl 3(4)), so it is fixed.
`the FTB Part A supplement income limit` MEANS 80000

-- Sch 2 cl 3(4): "upper income (base rate) threshold means the lower income (base rate) threshold plus $450,000" -- not indexed.
`the base rate band` MEANS 450000

§§ `6 -- the immunisation requirements`

-- s 6(1): when a child "meets the immunisation requirements" for CCS eligibility (Div 2 of Part 4A) and for the FTB child
-- rate reduction under Sch 1 cll 7(2), (3), 26(3), (4).
-- (2) "The child meets the immunisation requirements if the child has been immunised" -- s 3: immunised in accordance with a
-- standard or catch up vaccination schedule determined under s 4 (the schedule is not deposited; asked as a fact).
-- (3) a GP or listed specialist "has certified in writing" a medical contraindication or natural immunity; or the child is in
-- an approved vaccine study. (4) the vaccine is temporarily unavailable (Chief Medical Officer's certificate, and "the
-- Secretary is satisfied that the child would have been immunised"). (5) vaccinated overseas, certified equivalent, and all
-- other vaccinations received. (6) "the Secretary determines in writing that the child meets the immunisation requirements".
-- There is no other ground: no exemption for a parent's conscientious or religious objection.
DECLARE `My child's immunisation` HAS
    `immunised under a standard or catch up schedule`       IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 6(2)
    `medical contraindication certified`                    IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 6(3)(a)
    `natural immunity certified`                            IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 6(3)(b)
    `in an approved vaccine study`                          IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 6(3)(c)
    `vaccine temporarily unavailable as s 6(4) requires`    IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 6(4), incl. the Secretary's satisfaction
    `vaccinated overseas as s 6(5) requires`                IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 6(5)
    `the Secretary has determined that my child meets them` IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 6(6)
    `I object to vaccination`                               IS A BOOLEAN  -- read by nothing: no s 6 ground

@export Does my child meet the immunisation requirements (s 6)?
GIVEN `my child` IS A `My child's immunisation` @desc Your child's vaccinations, certificates and any Secretary's determination
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my child meet the immunisation requirements` IF
        `my child`'s `immunised under a standard or catch up schedule`
    OR  `my child`'s `medical contraindication certified`
    OR  `my child`'s `natural immunity certified`
    OR  `my child`'s `in an approved vaccine study`
    OR  `my child`'s `vaccine temporarily unavailable as s 6(4) requires`
    OR  `my child`'s `vaccinated overseas as s 6(5) requires`
    OR  `my child`'s `the Secretary has determined that my child meets them`

§§ `61B, Sch 1 cll 7(2), 26(3) -- what failing them does to my FTB`

-- s 61B(1)(b)(ii): the FTB child rate is reduced if the child does not meet the requirements, "for family tax benefit paid to
-- the individual in instalments--before the end of the grace period". (3) the Secretary "must give a notice". (4) the grace
-- period "(a) begins on the day specified as the date of the notice ... and (b) ends 63 days after that day".
-- (2) the FTB child rate reduction period "(a) begin[s] on the day specified as the date of the notice ... and (b) end[s] on
-- the day the child meets the immunisation requirements". Once the grace period is missed, the reduction runs from the
-- NOTICE date, not from the end of the grace period.
-- Meeting the requirements ON day 63 is treated as within the grace period (INFERENCE: "ends 63 days after that day").
@export Will my FTB child rate be reduced because my child did not meet the immunisation requirements in time (s 61B)?
GIVEN `met the requirements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your child has now met the immunisation requirements
      `days after the notice date when met` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days after the date of the Secretary's notice your child met them
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Will my FTB child rate be reduced` IF
    NOT (`met the requirements` AND `days after the notice date when met` AT MOST 63)

@export For how many days will my FTB child rate be reduced (s 61B(2))?
GIVEN `met the requirements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your child has now met the immunisation requirements
      `days after the notice date when met` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days after the date of the notice your child met them (or the days so far, if not yet met)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`For how many days will my FTB child rate be reduced` MEANS
    IF `Will my FTB child rate be reduced` `met the requirements` `days after the notice date when met`
    THEN `days after the notice date when met`
    ELSE 0

-- Sch 1 cl 7(2): "the annual FTB child rate in relation to the child is reduced by $737.30 for each day in the FTB child rate
-- reduction period" (Method 2: cl 26(3), same amount). s 61C keeps the entitlement alive at a nil rate; the floor at nil is
-- an INFERENCE from s 61C ("rate ... is nil as a result of section 61A or 61B").
@export What is my annual FTB child rate for my child on a day in the reduction period (Sch 1 cl 7(2))?
GIVEN `the rates` IS A Rates @desc The indexed rates in force
      `my child is 13 or over` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your child has reached 13
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my annual FTB child rate on a reduced day` MEANS
    `the positive part of`
        ((IF `my child is 13 or over`
          THEN `the rates`'s `FTB child rate (A1), child 13 or over`
          ELSE `the rates`'s `FTB child rate (A1), child under 13`)
         MINUS `the rates`'s `reduction in FTB child rate`)

§§ `21, 22, 26 -- am I eligible for family tax benefit`

-- s 22: an individual is an FTB child of the adult if
--   (2) "aged under 16", "in the adult's care", an Australian resident (or special category visa holder residing in Australia)
--       or "living with the adult", and legal responsibility as in (5)(a), (b) or (c); or
--   (3) "has turned 16 but is aged under 18", the same, and "a senior secondary school child"; or
--   (4) "aged 18 or is aged 19 and the calendar year in which the individual turned 19 has not ended", in care, resident or
--       living with the adult, and a senior secondary school child (no legal-responsibility limb).
-- (5) (a) the adult "is legally responsible (whether alone or jointly with someone else) for the day-to-day care, welfare and
-- development"; (b) a family law order or parenting plan says the child is to live or spend time with the adult; (c) no one
-- with that legal responsibility has the child. "senior secondary school child" is defined in s 3 (asked as a fact).
-- Nothing in s 22 asks whether the child's parents are married.
DECLARE `My child` HAS
    `age in years`                                   IS A NUMBER   -- s 22(2)(a), (3)(a), (4)(a)
    `in my care`                                     IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 22(2)(b)
    `an Australian resident or living with me`       IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 22(2)(c)
    `I have legal responsibility as s 22(5) requires` IS A BOOLEAN -- s 22(2)(d), (5)
    `a senior secondary school child`                IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 22(3)(e), (4)(d)
    `the calendar year my child turned 19 has ended` IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 22(4)(a)
    `my child's parents are married to each other`   IS A BOOLEAN  -- read by nothing

GIVEN `age` IS A NUMBER
      `the calendar year my child turned 19 has ended` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `aged 18, or 19 in the year of turning 19` IF
        `age` EQUALS 18
    OR  `age` EQUALS 19 AND NOT `the calendar year my child turned 19 has ended`

GIVEN `c` IS A `My child`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the age limb of s 22 is met` IF
        `c`'s `age in years` LESS THAN 16
            AND `c`'s `I have legal responsibility as s 22(5) requires`
    OR  `c`'s `age in years` AT LEAST 16
            AND `c`'s `age in years` LESS THAN 18
            AND `c`'s `I have legal responsibility as s 22(5) requires`
            AND `c`'s `a senior secondary school child`
    OR  `aged 18, or 19 in the year of turning 19` (`c`'s `age in years`) (`c`'s `the calendar year my child turned 19 has ended`)
            AND `c`'s `a senior secondary school child`

@export Is my child an FTB child of mine (s 22)?
GIVEN `my child` IS A `My child` @desc Your child's age, care, residence and schooling, and your legal responsibility
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my child an FTB child of mine` IF
        `my child`'s `in my care`
    AND `my child`'s `an Australian resident or living with me`
    AND `the age limb of s 22 is met` `my child`

-- s 21(1): eligible if "(a) ... has at least one FTB child"; "(b) ... is an Australian resident" (or a listed visa holder);
-- "(c) the individual's rate of family tax benefit ... is greater than nil". s 26(1): where 2 members of a couple would both
-- be eligible "only one member is eligible" -- the one the Secretary determines, having regard to who is primary carer and
-- any written nomination (s 26(2)); asked as a fact.
@export Am I eligible for family tax benefit (s 21)?
GIVEN `my child` IS A `My child` @desc Your child
      `I am an Australian resident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an Australian resident (or special category visa holder residing in Australia)
      `my annual FTB rate` IS A NUMBER @desc Your annual rate of FTB (Part A plus Part B) as worked out below
      `my partner is the member of the couple who is eligible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are in a couple and the Secretary has decided under s 26 that your partner, not you, is the one eligible
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I eligible for family tax benefit` IF
        `Is my child an FTB child of mine` `my child`
    AND `I am an Australian resident`
    AND `my annual FTB rate` GREATER THAN 0
    AND NOT `my partner is the member of the couple who is eligible`

§§ `Sch 1 Part 2, Part 3, cl 38A, Part 5 Div 2C; Sch 3 cl 3 -- how much FTB Part A`

-- The family, as the parent can state it. Children are counted by the cl 7(1) categories. "adjusted taxable income" is
-- worked out under Schedule 3 (taxable income plus fringe benefits, foreign income, net investment losses and so on); it is
-- asked as a figure for each partner. "newborn supplement" is the annual amount added under cl 35B for a day on which cl 35A
-- applies (the formula is absent from the deposit; 0 if none).
DECLARE `My family` HAS
    `FTB children under 13`                         IS A NUMBER   -- cl 7(1) item 1
    `FTB children 13 or over`                       IS A NUMBER   -- cl 7(1) item 2
    `age of my youngest FTB child`                  IS A NUMBER   -- cl 30, cl 28D
    `I am a member of a couple`                     IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 3: the Social Security Act 1991 meaning
    `my adjusted taxable income`                    IS A NUMBER   -- Sch 3 cl 2
    `my partner's adjusted taxable income`          IS A NUMBER   -- Sch 3 cl 3 (0 if single)
    `I or my partner get a pension or benefit`      IS A BOOLEAN  -- cl 1(2)(a)(ii), 38L, 28B(2)
    `newborn supplement in my rate`                 IS A NUMBER   -- cl 3 step 1(ba), cl 25 step 1(ba)
    `I am a grandparent of my youngest FTB child`   IS A BOOLEAN  -- cl 28D(2)
    `parental leave pay is payable to me or my partner for the day` IS A BOOLEAN  -- cl 28C

GIVEN `f` IS A `My family`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of FTB children` MEANS `f`'s `FTB children under 13` PLUS `f`'s `FTB children 13 or over`

-- Sch 3 cl 3(1): "For the purposes of this Act (other than Part 4 of Schedule 1), if an individual is a member of a couple,
-- the individual's adjusted taxable income ... includes the adjusted taxable income ... of the individual's partner."
@export What adjusted taxable income is my FTB Part A tested on (Sch 3 cl 3(1))?
GIVEN `f` IS A `My family` @desc Your family
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What income is my FTB Part A tested on` MEANS
    IF `f`'s `I am a member of a couple`
    THEN `f`'s `my adjusted taxable income` PLUS `f`'s `my partner's adjusted taxable income`
    ELSE `f`'s `my adjusted taxable income`

-- cl 1(2): "(a) use Part 2 ... if the individual has at least one FTB child and: (i) the individual's adjusted taxable income
-- does not exceed the individual's higher income free area; or (ii) the individual, or the individual's partner, is
-- receiving a social security pension, a social security benefit ...; (b) use Part 3 ... [otherwise]; (c) use Part 3A ...
-- if the individual has no FTB children" (Part 3A is rent assistance only, not encoded).
@export Is my FTB Part A worked out by Method 1 (Sch 1 cl 1(2))?
GIVEN `the rates` IS A Rates @desc The indexed rates in force
      `f` IS A `My family` @desc Your family
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my FTB Part A worked out by Method 1` IF
        `the number of FTB children` `f` AT LEAST 1
    AND (   `What income is my FTB Part A tested on` `f` AT MOST `the rates`'s `higher income free area`
         OR `f`'s `I or my partner get a pension or benefit`)

-- cl 38A: "(1A) ... nil if the individual's adjusted taxable income is more than $80,000"; "(1)(b) if the individual has 2
-- or more FTB children--the sum of the applicable supplement amounts"; (2)(b) the applicable amount is "the FTB gross
-- supplement amount"; (3) "$600". Shared care (2)(a) is not encoded.
GIVEN `the rates` IS A Rates
      `f` IS A `My family`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`my FTB Part A supplement` MEANS
    IF `What income is my FTB Part A tested on` `f` GREATER THAN `the FTB Part A supplement income limit`
    THEN 0
    ELSE `the number of FTB children` `f` TIMES `the rates`'s `FTB gross supplement amount (A)`

-- cl 3 step 1: the maximum rate is "(a) the individual's standard rate" (cl 7(1): the sum of the FTB child rates, $4,292.40
-- under 13 and $5,580.85 from 13) "(ba) ... newborn supplement (if any) ... (ca) ... FTB Part A supplement" (the multiple
-- birth allowance, energy supplement and rent assistance are not encoded).
@export What is my maximum rate of FTB Part A (Sch 1 cl 3 step 1)?
GIVEN `the rates` IS A Rates @desc The indexed rates in force
      `f` IS A `My family` @desc Your family
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my maximum rate of FTB Part A` MEANS
        `f`'s `FTB children under 13` TIMES `the rates`'s `FTB child rate (A1), child under 13`
    PLUS `f`'s `FTB children 13 or over` TIMES `the rates`'s `FTB child rate (A1), child 13 or over`
    PLUS `f`'s `newborn supplement in my rate`
    PLUS `my FTB Part A supplement` `the rates` `f`

-- cl 25 step 1: the Method 2 base rate is "(a) the individual's standard rate" (cl 26(2): "$1,416.20" per child) "(ba) ...
-- newborn supplement ... (d) ... FTB Part A supplement". cl 4: the base rate (Method 1) is the Method 2 base rate.
@export What is my base rate of FTB Part A (Sch 1 cll 4, 25 step 1)?
GIVEN `the rates` IS A Rates @desc The indexed rates in force
      `f` IS A `My family` @desc Your family
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my base rate of FTB Part A` MEANS
        `the number of FTB children` `f` TIMES `the rates`'s `FTB child rate (A2)`
    PLUS `f`'s `newborn supplement in my rate`
    PLUS `my FTB Part A supplement` `the rates` `f`

-- Method 1. cl 3 step 2 with cl 38M: "The individual's reduction for adjusted taxable income is 20% of the income excess"
-- over the income free area (cl 38N: "$40,000"); cl 38L: for a pension or benefit recipient "the individual's income excess
-- is nil". Step 3 (maintenance) is not encoded: maintenance income is taken to be nil. Step 4: "the individual's base rate
-- ... if it is more than the individual's income and maintenance tested rate".
-- Method 2. cl 25 step 2 with cl 28: "30% of the income excess" over the higher income free area (cl 2: "$98,988"), from the
-- Method 2 base rate: the provisional Part A rate. Step 3 with cl 25D: the maximum rate less "20% of" (HIFA less income free
-- area) and "30% of" (income less HIFA). Step 4: the greater of the two. The floor at nil is an INFERENCE (s 21(1)(c)
-- speaks of a rate "greater than nil"). No FTB child: Part 3A (rent assistance only) -- nil here.
@export How much FTB Part A do I get a year (Sch 1 cll 3, 25)?
GIVEN `the rates` IS A Rates @desc The indexed rates in force
      `f` IS A `My family` @desc Your family
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much FTB Part A do I get a year` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the number of FTB children` `f` EQUALS 0                   THEN 0
           IF `Is my FTB Part A worked out by Method 1` `the rates` `f`  THEN max `income tested rate` `base rate`
           OTHERWISE `the positive part of` (max `provisional Part A rate` `Method 2 income tested rate`)
    WHERE
        `income`       MEANS `What income is my FTB Part A tested on` `f`
        `maximum rate` MEANS `What is my maximum rate of FTB Part A` `the rates` `f`
        `base rate`    MEANS `What is my base rate of FTB Part A` `the rates` `f`
        `HIFA`         MEANS `the rates`'s `higher income free area`
        `IFA`          MEANS `the rates`'s `income free area (A)`
        `income tested rate` MEANS
            IF `f`'s `I or my partner get a pension or benefit`
            THEN `maximum rate`
            ELSE `maximum rate` MINUS `percent of` 20 (`the positive part of` (`income` MINUS `IFA`))
        `provisional Part A rate` MEANS
            `base rate` MINUS `percent of` 30 (`income` MINUS `HIFA`)
        `Method 2 income tested rate` MEANS
            `maximum rate` MINUS `percent of` 20 (`HIFA` MINUS `IFA`) MINUS `percent of` 30 (`income` MINUS `HIFA`)

§§ `Sch 1 Part 4; Sch 3 cl 3(2) -- how much FTB Part B`

-- Sch 3 cl 3(2): for Part 4 of Schedule 1, a member of a couple's adjusted taxable income is "(a) for the purposes of
-- Subdivision AA [cll 28B-28D] ... the adjusted taxable income ... of the individual's partner if it is more than the
-- individual's"; "(b) for the purposes of the other provisions ... the adjusted taxable income ... of the individual's partner
-- if it is less". So the $100,000 limit is tested on the higher earner and the income test on the lower earner.
@export What income is my FTB Part B limit tested on (Sch 3 cl 3(2)(a))?
GIVEN `f` IS A `My family` @desc Your family
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What income is my FTB Part B limit tested on` MEANS
    IF `f`'s `I am a member of a couple`
    THEN max (`f`'s `my adjusted taxable income`) (`f`'s `my partner's adjusted taxable income`)
    ELSE `f`'s `my adjusted taxable income`

@export What income is my FTB Part B income test applied to (Sch 3 cl 3(2)(b))?
GIVEN `f` IS A `My family` @desc Your family
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What income is my FTB Part B income test applied to` MEANS
    IF `f`'s `I am a member of a couple`
    THEN min (`f`'s `my adjusted taxable income`) (`f`'s `my partner's adjusted taxable income`)
    ELSE `f`'s `my adjusted taxable income`

-- Subdivision AA. cl 28B: "(1) ... Part B rate is nil if the individual's adjusted taxable income is more than $100,000";
-- "(2) ... does not apply while the individual, or the individual's partner, is receiving a social security pension ...".
-- cl 28C: "nil if the day is a day for which parental leave pay is payable to the individual, or the individual's partner".
-- cl 28D: nil if "(a) the individual is a member of a couple; and (b) the youngest FTB child of the individual has turned 13",
-- unless "(2) ... the individual is a grandparent or great-grandparent of that FTB child".
@export Is my FTB Part B nil (Sch 1 cll 28B-28D)?
GIVEN `the rates` IS A Rates @desc The indexed rates in force
      `f` IS A `My family` @desc Your family
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my FTB Part B nil` IF
        `the number of FTB children` `f` EQUALS 0
    OR  (    `What income is my FTB Part B limit tested on` `f` GREATER THAN `the rates`'s `income limit (B)`
         AND NOT `f`'s `I or my partner get a pension or benefit`)
    OR  `f`'s `parental leave pay is payable to me or my partner for the day`
    OR  (    `f`'s `I am a member of a couple`
         AND `f`'s `age of my youngest FTB child` AT LEAST 13
         AND NOT `f`'s `I am a grandparent of my youngest FTB child`)

-- cl 29(1) (not a member of a couple): the Part B rate is the standard rate (cl 30: "$2,569.60" if the "youngest FTB child is
-- under 5 years of age", "$1,781.20" if "5 years of age or over") plus the FTB Part B supplement (cl 31A(2): "$302.95")
-- (plus energy supplement (Part B), closed by cl 29AA, not encoded). No income test applies to a single parent beyond cl 28B.
-- cl 29(2) (member of a couple): that maximum rate less the reduction in cl 32: "20% of the income excess" over the income
-- free area (cl 33: "$4,000"), on the lower earner's income (Sch 3 cl 3(2)(b)). The floor at nil is an INFERENCE.
@export How much FTB Part B do I get a year (Sch 1 Part 4)?
GIVEN `the rates` IS A Rates @desc The indexed rates in force
      `f` IS A `My family` @desc Your family
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much FTB Part B do I get a year` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `Is my FTB Part B nil` `the rates` `f`  THEN 0
           IF `f`'s `I am a member of a couple`        THEN `the positive part of` (`maximum rate` MINUS `reduction`)
           OTHERWISE `maximum rate`
    WHERE
        `maximum rate` MEANS `my FTB Part B maximum rate` `the rates` `f`
        `reduction`    MEANS `percent of` 20 (`the positive part of` (`What income is my FTB Part B income test applied to` `f` MINUS `the rates`'s `income free area (B)`))

GIVEN `the rates` IS A Rates
      `f` IS A `My family`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`my FTB Part B maximum rate` MEANS
        (IF `f`'s `age of my youngest FTB child` LESS THAN 5
         THEN `the rates`'s `FTB standard rate (B), youngest under 5`
         ELSE `the rates`'s `FTB standard rate (B), youngest 5 or over`)
    PLUS `the rates`'s `FTB gross supplement amount (B)`

-- Sch 1 cl 1(1): "To work out an individual's annual rate of family tax benefit, add: (a) the individual's Part A rate ...;
-- and (b) the individual's Part B rate".
@export How much family tax benefit do I get a year (Sch 1 cl 1(1))?
GIVEN `the rates` IS A Rates @desc The indexed rates in force
      `f` IS A `My family` @desc Your family
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much family tax benefit do I get a year` MEANS
    `How much FTB Part A do I get a year` `the rates` `f` PLUS `How much FTB Part B do I get a year` `the rates` `f`

§§ `Sch 1 cl 35A -- the newborn supplement`

-- cl 35A(1): newborn supplement is added, for a day, to the maximum rate (or Method 2 base rate) if subclause (2), (5) or (7)
-- applies. (2) parent of the child: "(a) the individual, or the individual's partner, is a parent of the child on that day";
-- "(b) the child is aged less than one"; "(c) ... the individual's Part A rate ... would be greater than nil"; "(d) that day
-- occurs in the period of 13 weeks beginning on the first day that paragraphs (a) to (c) are satisfied"; "(e)" the birth
-- registration requirement is notified in time.
-- (8) "This clause does not apply, and is taken never to have applied, ... if parental leave pay is payable to the individual
-- for that child." (9) Nor if parental leave pay is payable to another person "for a flexible PPL day for that child" and
-- that person and the individual "are members of a couple on that day". (10) once added for 13 weeks to one member of a
-- couple (no s 28/29 determination), the clause does not apply to the other member.
-- "parental leave pay" and "flexible PPL day" have the Paid Parental Leave Act 2010 meanings (borrowed terms, asked as
-- facts). 13 weeks is counted as days 0 to 90 from the first qualifying day (INFERENCE about counting). Marriage is not read.
DECLARE `My newborn` HAS
    `I or my partner am a parent of the child`        IS A BOOLEAN  -- cl 35A(2)(a), (14)
    `the child is aged less than one`                 IS A BOOLEAN  -- (2)(b)
    `my Part A rate would be greater than nil`        IS A BOOLEAN  -- (2)(c)
    `days since the first qualifying day`             IS A NUMBER   -- (2)(d)
    `birth registration notified in time`             IS A BOOLEAN  -- (2)(e), (3)
    `parental leave pay is payable to me for the child` IS A BOOLEAN -- (8)
    `my partner is paid parental leave pay for a flexible PPL day` IS A BOOLEAN -- (9)
    `my partner already had the supplement for 13 weeks` IS A BOOLEAN -- (10)
    `the child's parents are married to each other`   IS A BOOLEAN  -- read by nothing

@export Is newborn supplement added to my FTB Part A for this day (Sch 1 cl 35A)?
GIVEN `n` IS A `My newborn` @desc Your newborn child and any parental leave pay
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is newborn supplement added for the day` IF
        `n`'s `I or my partner am a parent of the child`
    AND `n`'s `the child is aged less than one`
    AND `n`'s `my Part A rate would be greater than nil`
    AND `n`'s `days since the first qualifying day` AT LEAST 0
    AND `n`'s `days since the first qualifying day` LESS THAN 91
    AND `n`'s `birth registration notified in time`
    AND NOT `n`'s `parental leave pay is payable to me for the child`
    AND NOT `n`'s `my partner is paid parental leave pay for a flexible PPL day`
    AND NOT `n`'s `my partner already had the supplement for 13 weeks`

§§ `58AA -- the newborn upfront payment`

-- s 58AA(1): "If, under Division 1A of Part 5 of Schedule 1, an amount of newborn supplement is added in relation to an
-- individual and an FTB child of the individual, then the individual is entitled to be paid, as an amount of family tax
-- benefit, $500 in respect of the FTB child." Paid as a single lump sum (note). (2) not if another individual "has received
-- an amount under this section in respect of that child while the individual and the other individual were members of the
-- same couple". (4) "cannot receive more than one amount" per FTB child.
-- So the upfront payment follows the supplement: no supplement (for example because parental leave pay is payable, cl
-- 35A(8)), no upfront payment.
@export Am I entitled to the newborn upfront payment (s 58AA)?
GIVEN `n` IS A `My newborn` @desc Your newborn child and any parental leave pay
      `my partner already received it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your partner has already been paid it for this child while you were a couple
      `I already received it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have already been paid it for this child
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled to the newborn upfront payment` IF
        `Is newborn supplement added for the day` `n`
    AND NOT `my partner already received it`
    AND NOT `I already received it`

-- s 58AA(1A): where both members of a couple have the supplement on the first day under a s 28 or 29 determination, each
-- gets "$500 multiplied by the percentage applicable under that determination".
@export How much newborn upfront payment do I get (s 58AA(1), (1A))?
GIVEN `the rates` IS A Rates @desc The indexed rates in force
      `n` IS A `My newborn` @desc Your newborn child and any parental leave pay
      `my partner already received it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your partner has already been paid it for this child while you were a couple
      `I already received it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have already been paid it for this child
      `my percentage under a section 28 or 29 determination` IS A NUMBER @desc Your percentage under a s 28 or 29 determination shared with your partner (100 if there is none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much newborn upfront payment do I get` MEANS
    IF `Am I entitled to the newborn upfront payment` `n` `my partner already received it` `I already received it`
    THEN `percent of` `my percentage under a section 28 or 29 determination` (`the rates`'s `newborn upfront payment`)
    ELSE 0

§§ `85BA -- am I eligible for the Child Care Subsidy for a session`

-- s 85BA(1): eligible for CCS for a session of care if (a) at the time "(i) the child is an FTB child, or a regular care
-- child, of the individual or the individual's partner"; "(ii) the child is 13 or under and does not attend secondary
-- school" (or a prescribed class); "(iii) the child meets the immunisation requirements in section 6"; "(iv) the
-- individual, or the individual's partner, meets the residency requirements in section 85BB"; (b) a liability to pay "under a
-- complying written arrangement"; (c) the session is "provided in Australia" and "not provided as part of the compulsory
-- education program"; paragraphs (c)(iii), (d) and (e) (Minister's rules, Division 5) are taken as satisfied.
-- Contrast with FTB: an unimmunised child REDUCES the FTB child rate (s 61B) but REMOVES CCS eligibility altogether.
DECLARE `My child's session of care` HAS
    `an FTB or regular care child of mine or my partner's`  IS A BOOLEAN  -- (1)(a)(i)
    `13 or under and not at secondary school`               IS A BOOLEAN  -- (1)(a)(ii)
    `my child meets the immunisation requirements`          IS A BOOLEAN  -- (1)(a)(iii), s 6
    `I or my partner meet the residency requirements`       IS A BOOLEAN  -- (1)(a)(iv), s 85BB
    `I am liable under a complying written arrangement`     IS A BOOLEAN  -- (1)(b)
    `provided in Australia`                                 IS A BOOLEAN  -- (1)(c)(i)
    `part of the compulsory education program`              IS A BOOLEAN  -- (1)(c)(ii)

@export Am I eligible for the Child Care Subsidy for this session of care (s 85BA)?
GIVEN `the session` IS A `My child's session of care` @desc The session of care and your child
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I eligible for CCS for the session` IF
        `the session`'s `an FTB or regular care child of mine or my partner's`
    AND `the session`'s `13 or under and not at secondary school`
    AND `the session`'s `my child meets the immunisation requirements`
    AND `the session`'s `I or my partner meet the residency requirements`
    AND `the session`'s `I am liable under a complying written arrangement`
    AND `the session`'s `provided in Australia`
    AND NOT `the session`'s `part of the compulsory education program`

§§ `Sch 2 cll 3, 3A, 3B -- what percentage of my fees is subsidised`

-- cl 3(1) table: adjusted taxable income "equal to or below the lower income (base rate) threshold" -- "90%"; "above the
-- lower ... and below the upper" -- "see subclause (2)" [a formula, absent from the deposit: an input]; "equal to or above
-- the upper income (base rate) threshold" -- "0%". (4) lower threshold "$80,000"; upper "the lower income (base rate)
-- threshold plus $450,000". For a couple the income includes the partner's (Sch 3 cl 3AA, simplified to a whole year).
@export What is my basic CCS applicable percentage (Sch 2 cl 3)?
GIVEN `the rates` IS A Rates @desc The indexed rates in force
      `my family's adjusted taxable income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your adjusted taxable income, with your partner's if you are in a couple
      `the cl 3(2) taper percentage` IS A NUMBER @desc The percentage the cl 3(2) formula gives at your income (the formula is not in the deposit)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my basic CCS percentage` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `income` AT MOST `lower`                          THEN 90
           IF `income` AT LEAST `lower` PLUS `the base rate band` THEN 0
           OTHERWISE `the cl 3(2) taper percentage`
    WHERE
        `income` MEANS `my family's adjusted taxable income`
        `lower`  MEANS `the rates`'s `CCS lower income (base rate) threshold`

-- cl 3B(1)-(2): a child is a "higher rate child" for a session in a CCS fortnight if the child is "under 6 years of age on the
-- first Monday of the CCS fortnight" and is in CCS by fee reduction for the individual, and another child who is also under
-- 6 and in CCS by fee reduction for the individual or partner is older (or, if born the same day, ranked above it by the
-- Secretary). The fee-reduction determinations are asked as facts.
@export Is my child a higher rate child for CCS (Sch 2 cl 3B)?
GIVEN `my child is under 6 and in CCS for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether this child is under 6 on the first Monday of the fortnight and you are eligible for CCS by fee reduction for the child
      `an older child under 6 is in CCS for me or my partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an older child (also under 6) is in CCS by fee reduction for you or your partner, or one born the same day is ranked above this child
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my child a higher rate child` IF
    `my child is under 6 and in CCS for me` AND `an older child under 6 is in CCS for me or my partner`

-- cl 3A(1): applies if "(a) the child is a higher rate child ...; (b) the session of care is not provided by an in home care
-- service; and (c) the individual's adjusted taxable income ... is below the upper income (other rate) threshold".
-- (2) if cl 3 would give a higher percentage, that is the percentage. (3) table: at or below the lower (other rate)
-- threshold "95%"; to the second threshold "see subclause (4)" [lesser of 95% and a formula]; second to third "80%"; third
-- to fourth "see subclause (5)" [a formula]; fourth to upper "50%". (6) lower "$72,466"; second = lower + $105,000; third =
-- lower + $184,290; fourth = lower + $274,290; upper = lower + $284,290. The formulas are absent from the deposit: inputs.
DECLARE `Service type` IS ONE OF
    `centre-based day care`
    `family day care`
    `outside school hours care`
    `in home care`

@export What is my CCS applicable percentage for this child (Sch 2 cll 3, 3A)?
GIVEN `the rates` IS A Rates @desc The indexed rates in force
      `my family's adjusted taxable income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your adjusted taxable income, with your partner's if you are in a couple
      `the service` IS A `Service type` @desc The kind of child care service
      `my child is a higher rate child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the child is a higher rate child (see the question above)
      `the cl 3(2) taper percentage` IS A NUMBER @desc The percentage the cl 3(2) formula gives at your income
      `the cl 3A(4) formula percentage` IS A NUMBER @desc The percentage the cl 3A(4) formula gives at your income
      `the cl 3A(5) formula percentage` IS A NUMBER @desc The percentage the cl 3A(5) formula gives at your income
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my CCS percentage` MEANS
    IF     `my child is a higher rate child`
       AND NOT `the service` EQUALS `in home care`
       AND `my family's adjusted taxable income` LESS THAN `lower other` PLUS 284290
    THEN max `basic` `other`
    ELSE `basic`
    WHERE
        `lower other` MEANS `the rates`'s `CCS lower income (other rate) threshold`
        `income`      MEANS `my family's adjusted taxable income`
        `basic`       MEANS `What is my basic CCS percentage` `the rates` `income` `the cl 3(2) taper percentage`
        `other`       MEANS
            BRANCH IF `income` AT MOST   `lower other`               THEN 95
                   IF `income` LESS THAN `lower other` PLUS 105000 THEN min 95 `the cl 3A(4) formula percentage`
                   IF `income` LESS THAN `lower other` PLUS 184290 THEN 80
                   IF `income` LESS THAN `lower other` PLUS 274290 THEN `the cl 3A(5) formula percentage`
                   OTHERWISE 50

§§ `Sch 2 cl 2 -- my hourly rate of CCS`

-- cl 2(1): the hourly rate of CCS is "the individual's applicable percentage ... of the lower of: (a) the hourly session fee
-- for the individual; and (b) the CCS hourly rate cap for the session; rounded to the nearest cent". (3) the caps:
-- centre-based day care "$11.98", family day care "$11.10", outside school hours care "$10.48", in home care "$32.58".
-- Rounding is not encoded (the cases use figures that need none).
GIVEN `the rates` IS A Rates
      `the service` IS A `Service type`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the CCS hourly rate cap` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the service`
    WHEN `centre-based day care`     THEN `the rates`'s `CCS hourly rate cap, centre-based day care`
    WHEN `family day care`           THEN `the rates`'s `CCS hourly rate cap, family day care`
    WHEN `outside school hours care` THEN `the rates`'s `CCS hourly rate cap, outside school hours care`
    WHEN `in home care`              THEN `the rates`'s `CCS hourly rate cap, in home care`

@export What is my hourly rate of CCS (Sch 2 cl 2)?
GIVEN `the rates` IS A Rates @desc The indexed rates in force
      `the service` IS A `Service type` @desc The kind of child care service
      `my percentage` IS A NUMBER @desc Your applicable percentage
      `the hourly session fee` IS A NUMBER @desc What you are charged per hour of the session
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my hourly rate of CCS` MEANS
    `percent of` `my percentage` (min `the hourly session fee` (`the CCS hourly rate cap` `the rates` `the service`))

§§ `Sch 2 cll 11, 12 -- how many hours are subsidised (the activity test)`

-- cl 11(1)(a): the subsidised hours for a CCS fortnight are "the highest of (i) the 3 day guarantee ... and (ii) any other
-- result" in the table in (1B); (b) for a member of a couple, "the lower of" the individual's and the partner's results.
-- (1A) "The 3 day guarantee for an individual for a CCS fortnight, in relation to any child, is 72."
-- cl 12(1) "The increased hours result is 100." (1A) it applies "if the individual engages in more than 48 hours of a
-- recognised participation type in the CCS fortnight" -- paid work, training, approved study, or prescribed or determined
-- types (12(2)); how hours are counted may be set by the Minister's rules (12(4)), not deposited: the hours are asked as a
-- fact. Other results (Minister's rules, child wellbeing, exceptional circumstances, Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander
-- child 100) are not encoded.
GIVEN `participation hours` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`one parent's result` MEANS
    IF `participation hours` GREATER THAN 48 THEN 100 ELSE 72

@export How many hours of child care are subsidised for me each fortnight (Sch 2 cll 11, 12)?
GIVEN `my recognised activity hours in the fortnight` IS A NUMBER @desc Hours of paid work, training or approved study you do in the fortnight
      `my partner's recognised activity hours in the fortnight` IS A NUMBER @desc The same for your partner (0 if none)
      `I am a member of a couple` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have a partner
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How many hours are subsidised each fortnight` MEANS
    IF `I am a member of a couple`
    THEN min (`one parent's result` `my recognised activity hours in the fortnight`)
             (`one parent's result` `my partner's recognised activity hours in the fortnight`)
    ELSE `one parent's result` `my recognised activity hours in the fortnight`

§§ `Sch 2 cll 1, 4 -- how much CCS for a fortnight`

-- cl 1: the amount of CCS for a week is worked out from the subsidised hours for the fortnight and the hourly rate for each
-- eligible session. cl 4(1)(a): "multiplying the hourly rate of CCS for the session by the number of hours in the session,
-- up to ... the balance of the subsidised hours". Simplified here to one service, one hourly fee and no other CCS hours in
-- the fortnight: the subsidy is the hourly rate times the lower of the hours of care and the subsidised hours. cl 4A (fee
-- below the subsidy) is not encoded.
@export How much Child Care Subsidy do I get for a fortnight (Sch 2 cll 1, 4)?
GIVEN `my hourly rate of CCS` IS A NUMBER @desc Your hourly rate of CCS
      `hours of care in the fortnight` IS A NUMBER @desc Hours of eligible sessions of care in the fortnight
      `my subsidised hours` IS A NUMBER @desc Your subsidised hours for the fortnight
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much CCS do I get for the fortnight` MEANS
    `my hourly rate of CCS` TIMES (min `hours of care in the fortnight` `my subsidised hours`)
